00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:34.820
And many of us in America right now are easily
triggered by the propagandists on our side

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:35.820
of the aisle.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:44.220
I know that I catch myself all the time overreacting
to the fear mongering of the some of the progressive

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:49.140
activists that I tend to trust and respect.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:55.260
Speaker 1: What about situations where maybe
two people with different views enter to a

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:59.600
conversation in good faith, really wanting
to sort of like hash out what what is the

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:00.600
truth?

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:04.330
And you get to the situation where it's sort
of like my source versus your source.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:08.920
And we get through these initial steps where
we ask the questions on what are you basing

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:09.920
your view on?

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:11.100
And I tell you what I'm basing my view on.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.440
And you tell me and the source is just sort
of conflict.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:18.490
And of course, a really deep study might show
