00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:44.930
of patience that we seem to have forgotten
the virtue of in this in these breakneck times.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:49.550
But but in principle, every one of us now
can fact check things by pulling a device

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:52.680
out of our pockets and starting to Google
things.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:56.540
But the thing to understand is that there's
a ton of unreliable information out there

00:11:56.540 --> 00:12:04.410
and a lot of it is on very slick websites
or in carefully manipulated statistical analyzes

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:10.450
so as to get you to support one or another
political or religious ideology.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.450
Right.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:14.530
So so you need to be very skeptical.

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:19.680
You need to look closely at the sources you
tend to rely on, both online and in the mainstream

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:25.040
media and and do your fact checking to find
out which ones are really reliable and ask

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:31.990
yourself who benefits from peddling this kind
of information and and what what incentives

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:36.720
might they have for skewing it in a way that
that might manipulate me?

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:42.140
Speaker 1: Last thing I wanted to ask you
about there, there's sometimes there's talk

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:45.630
of sort of like benign conspiratorial beliefs.

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:50.000
And often the one that's cited is like flat
earth as an example, someone who believes

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:51.770
flat earth, it's OK.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:55.960
You know, it's kind of wacky, but it really
is not damaging.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:13:01.510
But then the counter that I've heard frequently
is someone who believes that likely doesn't

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:07.790
believe only that and flat earth and anti-Semitism
