00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:13.030
How should we evaluate, like which battles
are worth fighting and and sort of adjudicating

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:18.450
some of the because there's just so much that
could be focused on and kind of thinking through

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.440
that fantastic question.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:26.510
Speaker 5: David, so a Canadian research team
just came out last year with a study that

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:32.001
shows that if you indulge in irresponsible
thinking in one domain, you weaken your mother's

00:13:32.001 --> 00:13:38.250
immune system in ways that compromised your
ability to distinguish fact from fiction in

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.320
other domains.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.320
Right.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:49.560
So if you indulge in wishful thinking for
the sake of of of harmony with your coreligionists,

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:55.120
you end up becoming more susceptible to conspiracy,
thinking more susceptible to science denial,

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.500
more susceptible to propaganda.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:03.200
So you can't say, oh, I'll just go off and
indulge in wishful thinking in this domain

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:09.570
and expect it not to compromise your mental
function.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:15.010
So I actually argue in the book that there's
our minds have a linch, our mental immune

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:18.940
systems have a linchpin, and that linchpin
is.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:25.540
Always yield to the better reason, never let
wishful thinking dissuade you from doing the

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:31.780
right thing, which is to believe as much as
possible on the basis of the best reasons

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:33.980
and evidence available.

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:40.840
So when you begin to move away from evidence
based thinking, you start to compromise your

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:47.130
minds, your mind's immune functioning, and
don't think you can only go a little ways

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:50.230
down this path and.

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:55.550
And not slide further down that path because
the evidence shows that the slope can become

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:56.550
very slippery.

00:14:56.550 --> 00:15:02.550
Speaker 1: Yeah, it seems like sometimes going
to a slippery slope is itself fallacious.

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:07.330
But in this case, it seems to really be a
core, a core aspect of how that works.

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:12.440
The book is called Mental Immunity Infectious
Ideas Mind Parasites and the Search for a

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:13.890
